Subject: [PATCH] Fix visual composition gap vs axis-shine reference
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Your screenshot of the live site showed a real, valid problem: the
earlier design patch only swapped color tokens and fonts, but never
did the actual composition work (elevation, spacing rhythm, nav
grouping) that makes axis-shine feel like a considered product rather
than "default shadcn with new colors." This closes that specific gap,
based on directly reading axis-shine's actual component source
(stat-card.tsx, app-shell.tsx, styles.css) rather than guessing.

- app/globals.css: --radius bumped from 0.375rem to 0.75rem (axis-shine's
  actual base radius). Added .panel utility (real two-stop shadow,
  matching axis-shine's --shadow-card exactly) and .numeric utility
  (tabular-nums) — previously missing entirely.
- components/ui/card.tsx: strengthened the base Card's shadow/radius to
  match .panel. This is the single highest-leverage fix, since Card is
  used everywhere (dashboard widgets, dialogs, every list page) — one
  change propagates real elevation app-wide instead of needing to touch
  every file that renders a card.
- components/dashboard/StatCard.tsx: rebuilt to match axis-shine's actual
  stat-card.tsx composition — .panel treatment, pill-shaped trend badge
  with arrow icon (was plain colored text), proper spacing rhythm
  (mt-3/mt-2/gap-0.5, matching axis-shine's exact values).
- components/layouts/AppSidebar.tsx: nav items restructured into labeled
  sections (Overview / Workspace / System) with uppercase tracked-wide
  labels, matching axis-shine's grouped-nav pattern — previously a flat
  unlabeled list, which was one of the more visually obvious gaps in the
  screenshot.

Kept the flush (non-floating-card) shell layout per explicit direction
to avoid the "SaaSy" floating-shell look axis-shine uses — this patch
adds real composition/elevation without reintroducing that.

Verified: tsc --noEmit clean, eslint clean on all touched files.
